00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:06,440
至少宣传手册上
是这么吹嘘的。
Or, at least, that's what
it said in the brochure.

392
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:09,800
但说老实话，
我根本就试不出半点区别。
But to be honest,
I just can't really
tell the difference.

393
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:13,200
所以，我宁可省下这830镑，
So, I'm saving my 830 quid

394
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,280
拿去买一堆美式橡皮糖吃。
and spending it
on American hard gums.

395
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,640
我还没吐槽完呢。
And I haven't finished yet.

396
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:26,120
话说上一代5系最出名的，
就是它的电脑算力
Now, the old 5 Series
famously had more
computing power

397
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:29,520
比当年飞去月球的
阿波罗飞船还要强。
than theApollo space craft
that went to the moon.

398
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:35,240
而这台车显然已经打算
“勇踏前人未至之境”了。
But this one seems to be
boldly going where no
executive car has gone before.

399
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:38,880
中控台上绝大部分按键
都被一块电视屏幕，
Most of the dashboard
buttons have been replaced
by a TV screen

400
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:42,160
以及底下这么个倒扣的
馅饼盘子给取代了。
and this sort of upturned
pie dish down here.

401
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,600
它掌控着车上的一切：
It controls everything:

402
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:48,640
空调、音响、卫星导航，
the air conditioning,
the stereo, the sat nav,

403
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:53,360
甚至晚上停好车后，
车灯还能亮多久都归它管。
even how long
the lights stay on after
you've parked up at night.

404
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:57,680
不过我最中意的还是这个，
某种倒车雷达显示器。
This is my favourite,
though. It's a sort of
radar parking device.

405
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,880
[有节奏的哔哔声]
[RHYTHMIC BEEPING]

406
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,600
平时停车，我都是专挑那种特别好停的位子，
Normally, I look for
really easy parking spaces,

407
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:08,760
但在宝马里，我专挑刁钻难停的，
就图个乐子。
but in the BMW,
I look for the tricky ones,
just for the fun of it.

408
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:16,360
搞定，停进去了。
So, there we go.

409
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:19,440
开着棒极了，
还自带一个电子游戏厅。
It's great to drive,
and it comes with its own
amusement arcade.

410
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:22,640
5系依然是一辆极好的车，
The 5 Series is still
a very good car,

411
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:26,720
依然是德国工程学的杰作。
still a great piece
of German engineering.

412
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:31,080
只是它把以前汤姆·克鲁斯那种
人见人爱的帅气长相，
It's just that it's exchanged
the easily digestible
looks of Tom Cruise

413
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:35,000
换成了那个叫杰拉尔·德帕迪约的家伙
那种……更有挑战性的面相。
for the more challenging
physiognomy of that
Gerard Dupedieu bloke.

414
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,320
那么，对手们又如何呢？
So, what about the rivals?

415
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,000
有捷豹S-Type。
There's the Jaguar S-Type.

416
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:50,720
开起来很爽，
但你瞧瞧它那张脸。
A great drive,
but look at its face.

417
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:56,120
还有奔驰E级，
老人家退休养老的绝佳座驾。
And there's the Mercedes
E-Class, a fabulous car
for your retirement.

418
00:22:56,160 --> 00:23:00,520
以前买5系，
向来被认为是不带脑子闭眼买的事。
Choosing a 5 Series
used to be considered
a bit of a no-brainer.

419
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:02,040
现在依然如此。
It still is.

420
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:09,040
你录那段片子的时候，脑子是哪儿不舒服吗？
Were you in any way unwell
when you recorded that?

421
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,440
呃，说实话，我当时确实病得不轻。
Well, actually, I did have
a really bad dose of the pox.

422
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:13,440
这就说得通了，因为……
That explains it, because

423
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,840
任何一双眼睛……
anybody whose eyes
were working

424
00:23:15,880 --> 00:23:18,280
好使的人都能看出，这是史上最丑的……
properly would recognise
that this is the ugliest...

425
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:20,280
-[观众叹气]
-它本来就是！
-[GROANS]
-It is!

426
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:21,960
-这车长相绝了，超级帅！
-这是有史以来第一辆……
-It is a superb-looking car.
-It's the first car ever

427
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,920
……能让小孩还没坐进后排就先被恶心吐的车！
where children will be sick
before they get in the back.

428
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,000
扯淡！
Rubbish!

429
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,240
-我们来举手表决。
-来就来。
-We'll have a vote.
-All right.

430
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,680
觉得它丑的，举手！
Hands up,
everyone who thinks it's ugly.

431
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:31,880
我可没暗中教唆他们啊。
I didn't prompt them
or anything.

432
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:36,320
现在，觉得它不丑的举手。
Now, hands up those
who think it's not ugly.

433
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:39,000
-瞧见没？举手的全把眼镜忘在家里了！
-行吧。
-You see? All the ones who've
left their glasses at home!
-All right.

434
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:41,640
行行行。假设你是个企业高管。
All right, all right.
You are an executive.

435
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,360
这对你来说可能得动用点想象力了。
This is gonna take
a bit of imagination.

436
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,920
你是个高管，好吧，你打算去买辆新车。
You're an executive, okay,
and you're gonna buy
a new car.

437
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:48,240
-你总不可能去买捷豹S-Type吧？
-不会。
-You're not going to buy
the S-Type Jag, are you?
-No.

438
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,120
开着确实不错，但你肯定不想
自家的孩子……
It's a great drive,
but you wouldn't let
your kids sit around

439
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,200
-整天跟它一样张着大嘴傻愣着。
-确实不想。
-with their mouths
open like that.
-No.

440
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,240
奔驰E级呢？
E-Class Mercedes.

441
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:55,840
我说，你不是有台奔驰吗？
这个夏天开得
有多爽啊？
Now, you've got a Mercedes.
How much have you enjoyed it
over the summer?

442
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:59,480
爽个屁。
它整个夏天
都泡在修车厂里。
No, I haven't.
It's been in the shop
the entire time.

443
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:02,240
送进去修，是坏的。
修完送回来，坏得更彻底，
然后又得送回去。
It goes in, it's broken.
It comes back more broken
and goes in again.

444
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,880
-没错。
-这就是当奔驰车主的
真实写照。
-Right.
-And that's pretty much
Mercedes ownership.

445
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,640
-所以，你肯定不会买它了？
-不买。
-So, you're not having
one of those?
-No.

446
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:07,480
-你也不会买奥迪A6，因为它太老气。
-呃，不买。
-You're not having an Audi A6
'cause it's too old.
-Er, no.

447
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,960
-你也不会买起亚远舰，因为太蠢了。
-没准我会买呢。
-You're not having a Kia
Magentis 'cause it's stupid.
-I might.

448
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,760
-拉倒吧，你才不会。
-好吧，你说得对。
我绝不会买。
-No, you wouldn't.
-No, you're right.
I wouldn't.

449
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:13,560
你也不会买阿尔法·罗密欧166，
And you're not
gonna have an Alfa 166

450
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:15,240
-因为压根没人会买新车。
-确实。
-because nobody
would buy a new one.
-No.

451
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,160
而你，杰里米·克拉克森，
You, Jeremy Clarkson,

452
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:21,280
作为全欧洲复印机
碳粉分销业务主管，
you are the European
director of Photocopying
[Toner Distribution].

453
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:23,920
你非得买这辆不可。
You will buy one of these.

454
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:27,280
我突然决定，
一个字都不想
再跟你废话了。
I've suddenly decided
I don't want to talk
to you any more.

455
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:30,240
我现在想做的，
是去采访今晚的嘉宾。
What I want to do
is talk to my guest tonight.

456
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:32,960
他曾是个摇滚巨星，但跟
别的摇滚明星不一样，
He was a rock star, but
unlike any other rock star,

457
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:36,960
他没倒在满是药丸和应召女郎的
酒店房间里，
淹死在一滩呕吐物中。
he didn't die in a pool
of vomit in a hotel room
full of pills and hookers.

458
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:41,640
恰恰相反，他在一场车祸中
葬身于冲天大火里。
Instead, he died
in an enormous fireball
in a car crash.

459
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:43,120
尽管如此，
他今晚还是来到了现场。
Despite this,
he's with us tonight.

460
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:45,200
女士们先生们，
掌声欢迎马丁·坎普！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Martin Kemp!

461
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,960
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

462
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,520
-最近怎么样？
-挺好的。
-How are you?
-Very well.

463
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:52,960
很好，请坐。
Good. Have a seat.

464
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:59,560
-噢。
-这么说，你之前在车祸里被撞死了。
-Ooh.
-So, you were killed
in a car crash.

465
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:01,160
-对啊。
-结果你居然还健在！
-Yeah.
-And you're still here!

466
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,640
是啊，我又杀回来了。
Yeah. And I'm back.

467
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:04,720
-撞的是宝马635。
-对。
-635 BM.
-Yeah.

468
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:07,960
你就不能挑一辆
没那么好的车去撞吗？
Couldn't you have smashed up
something a little bit less
good than that?

469
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:11,680
[笑] 哎，确实，
不过这有时正是当演员的
妙处所在嘛。
[LAUGHS] Well, yeah,
but that's the beauty,
sometimes, of being an actor.

470
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:13,880
你可以把这种顶呱呱的好车
撞得稀巴烂，你懂的。
You smash up
these really nice cars,
you know.

471
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:16,760
能从里面得到某种
变态的施虐快感。
Some kind of sadistic pleasure
you get from it.

472
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:20,600
那我能为你下一部戏
推荐一辆拿去撞的新车吗？
Can I offer you
a new car to smash up
in your next venture?

473
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:22,440
-全新宝马5系。
-[笑]
-The new 5 Series BMW.
-[LAUGHS]

474
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:24,080
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

475
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:26,360
你跟罗斯·坎普一样，都以车祸戏退场，
You, like Ross Kemp,
left in a car accident,

476
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,680
-你跳槽去了ITV台，也跟罗斯·坎普一样……
-对。
-you've gone to ITV,
like Ross Kemp...
-Yep.

477
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:30,400
-你们俩还都姓坎普。
-对。
-You're both called Kemp.
-Yep.

478
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:32,800
他上过我们节目，现在你也来了。
He's been on this show,
now you're on it.

479
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:35,640
这难道意味着
你接下来要跟
皮尔斯·摩根结婚了？
Does that mean
you're now going
to marry Piers Morgan?

480
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:37,840
[笑]
我跟你说实话吧。
[LAUGHS]
I'll tell you something.

481
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:41,400
当年我刚离开《东区人》剧组，
跳槽去ITV的时候，
When I first left EastEnders
and I joined ITV,

482
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:43,080
兜里总算有了俩闲钱，
I had a few quid
in my pocket,

483
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:45,160
我就琢磨着，“妥了，
必须得好好犒劳犒劳自己”。
and I thought, "Right,
I'm gonna treat myself".

484
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:48,840
于是我就直奔
当地一家专卖911的车行，
保时捷车行，
So, I went down to
the local 911 garage,
Porsche garage,

485
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,800
我站在那儿，
and I'm standing there

486
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,680
正趴在一辆车的车窗往里瞅呢，
and looking in a window
of a car, you know,

487
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:55,000
突然有人从后面拍了拍我的背。
and someone touched
my back here.

488
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:58,960
结果回头一看，隔壁那辆车窗前
站着罗斯，也是来买保时捷的！
And looking in the window here
of the next car is Ross,
buying his Porsche!

489
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,640
我当时就想：“得，跳出《东区人》
待遇果然立竿见影啊”。
So, I thought, "Well, that's
what you get if you leave
EastEnders",you know.

490
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:04,000
所以你买的是911 Turbo？
So, you've got
a 911 turbo?

491
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:05,400
不，不是Turbo。
No, not a turbo.

492
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:07,240
-但他买的是Turbo。
-没错。
-But he's got a turbo.
-Yeah.

493
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,840
不过人家身板块头大嘛。
He's a big boy, though.

494
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:11,280
少来，
你哪能容忍他开Turbo压你一头！
Now, come on.
You can't allow him
to have a turbo!

495
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:14,440
-那你呢……
你买的到底是哪款？
-我买的是Carrera。
-And you...
What have you got, then?
-I've got a Carrera.

496
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:15,640
-挺不错的。
-Carrera……
-It's lovely.
-Carrera...

497
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,480
反正就是911。
It's 911.

498
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:19,680
你看，
那到底是Carrera 2，
还是……
Now, you see,
is it a Carrera 2,
or is it...

499
00:26:19,720 --> 00:26:22,280
我告诉你到底是哪款吧，
黑色的那款。
I'll tell you
which one it is.
It's the black one.

500
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:23,200
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

501
00:26:25,080 --> 00:26:27,440
不过说真的，
我前前后后买过不少911。
But, yeah, I've had
a long line of 911s.

502
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:30,320
当年我搞乐队时买的第一辆车就是911。
My first car when
I was in a band was a 911.

503
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:33,400
这些年算下来，
我大概买过八辆吧。
I think, over the years,
I've had about eight of them.

504
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:36,000
但说实话，
新款911挺让我失望的。
But the new ones
I'm kind of disappointed in.

505
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:37,960
-现在的款式有点……
-有点太软绵绵了？
-These ones are kind of...
-A bit too soft?

506
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,000
-没错。
-我倒还挺……
-Yes.
-I quite...

507
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:42,960
不知不觉就挂上五挡（Fifth Gear）了，
开起来毫无挑战性。
Before you know it,
you're up in fifth gear,
and it's too easy to drive.

508
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,560
对，我个人还是更喜欢挂进“最高挡”（Top Gear）。
Yeah. I prefer to get
into top gear myself.

509
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:46,240
-[笑]
-不过，呃……
-[LAUGHS]
-But, um...

510
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,360
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

511
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:51,120
-顺带损了一把隔壁对手节目啊。
-相当精彩。
-Having a bit of a dig
at the opposition there.
-Very good.

512
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:54,200
那你人生第一辆车就是911吗？
Did you start off
with 911 then?

513
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:56,480
不是，我最早开的是蓝旗亚，
开了几个月。
Yeah, I started off with
a Lancia that I had
for a few months.

514
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:58,400
哟，蓝旗亚我喜欢。哪一款？
Ooh. I like that. Which one?

515
00:26:58,440 --> 00:27:02,240
就是车顶带硬顶，
后面……
It was the one
with the hard top
on the roof...

516
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:05,280
-我知道，能折叠……
是Beta吗？
-后窗可以折叠放倒的那款。
-I know. The folded...
It was a Beta?
-Folding back window.

517
00:27:05,320 --> 00:27:07,320
不是Coupe版，是Beta。
Not the coupe, the Beta.

518
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,320
-Beta。
-那个留胡子的家伙跑哪去了？
-The Beta.
-Where's that man
with the beard?

519
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:11,040
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

520
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:13,200
不是Monte Carlo，
那款是中置引擎的。
Not the Monte Carlo.
That was the one
that was mid engine.

521
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,640
蓝旗亚Beta，
带后车窗的那款。
The Lancia Beta,
with the back window.

522
00:27:14,680 --> 00:27:16,000
确实是Beta，
但具体来说……
It was a Beta,
but specifically...

523
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:18,080
-大胡子哪儿去了？
-Spider？是Spider版吗？
-Where's Beardy?
-Spider? Was it a Spider?

524
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:19,960
-叫什么来着？Spider！
-Spider！
-What was it called? Spider!
-Spider!

525
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,480
我们都知道Beta……
行了行了，闹够了！
We know the Beta...
Now, all right, that's enough!

526
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:23,720
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

527
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:27,080
-就是Beta Spider。
-Beta Spider。
-It was the Beta Spider.
-Beta Spider.

528
00:27:27,120 --> 00:27:29,480
我很喜欢它，你知道的，
我开过几个月。
I loved it, you know, and
I had that for a few months.

529
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:31,520
它有没有……呃其实没有，
不然早就
氧化生锈了。
Did it... Well, actually no,
then it would have
oxidised.

530
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:33,440
确实。[笑]
Yeah. [LAUGHS]

531
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:37,600
后来，我出门
买了辆911E，
那是我第一辆保时捷。
And then, I went out
and bought a 911E,
which was my first Porsche.

532
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:38,880
但你不是还有过一辆944吗？
But didn't you have a 944?

533
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:41,080
呃，我有过一辆，
大概就开了一天。
Well, I had one
for about a day.

534
00:27:41,120 --> 00:27:45,720
我特别迷911，
我记得一口气
接连买了四辆。
I was into 911s,
and I think I had about
four of them on the trot.

535
00:27:45,760 --> 00:27:49,600
后来我觉得
该换换口味了，于是出门
买了辆944。
And then, I thought
I needed a change, so I went
out and bought a 944.

536
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:51,240
我爸妈住在多塞特郡，
My mum and dad
lived down in Dorset,

537
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:53,480
有一天我就开着它
去了一趟。
so I drove it
down there one day.

538
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:55,920
回程路上我越开越失望，
I was so disappointed with it
on the way back

539
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:58,080
索性把车拐进一家保时捷车行，
又买了辆911。
that I stopped
in the 911 garage
and bought another one.

540
00:27:58,120 --> 00:27:59,640
所以，呃……
So, um...

541
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:00,800
-就开了24小时。
-所以，只撑了一天？
-It was 24 hours.
-So, it lasted one day?

542
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:04,120
-对！没错。
-真是笔划算的二手交易！
-Yeah! Yep.
-Good second-hand buy!

543
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:06,800
话说回来，在路上开车时，
到底什么最让你火大？
Anyway, on the roads,
what is it that gets you
really going?

544
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,960
行吧，有两件事最让我恼火。
All right, there's
two things that get me.

545
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,400
-一个是M4高速上的公交车道……
-对。
-One is the bus lane
on the M4...
-Yeah.

546
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:14,440
……另一个就是
开四驱车接送孩子上下学。
...and the other
is the 4x4 trip to school.

547
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:15,840
四驱车接送大军。
The school run, 4x4.

548
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:18,200
对。那平时是你去接送孩子吗？
Yeah. So, do you do
the school run?

549
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,760
-是的，我去。
-那你开什么车？
-I do, yeah.
-And what car have you got?

550
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,720
-四驱车。
-[观众大笑]
-4x4.
-[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

551
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:27,280
你去接送孩子没什么困扰吗？
Is it okay
doing the school run for you?

552
00:28:27,320 --> 00:28:29,600
呃，其实这是我自己
想做的事，
Well, it's something
that I want to do

553
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:31,480
因为我觉得
总得让……
because I think
you have to show...

554
00:28:31,520 --> 00:28:34,120
呃，我得让孩子们体会到
正常的生活。
Well, I have to show my kids
some kind of normality.

555
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:36,560
而且因为……
And because...

556
00:28:36,600 --> 00:28:38,840
但我猜校门口的那些妈妈们，
反应肯定很不正常。
But I would imagine that
the women at the school gates
don't react in a normal way.

557
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:40,600
-[轻笑]
-要是你们看到他
出现在校门口……
-[CHUCKLES]
-If you saw him
rocking up...

558
00:28:40,640 --> 00:28:42,280
你们能保持淡定吗？
Would you react
in a normal way?

559
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:44,480
-难道会说：
“早上好，肯普先生”？
-我会尖叫。
-Would you say,
"Good morning, Mr Kemp?"
-I'd scream.

560
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,960
-克拉克森：你会尖叫。
那么，现在……
-是的。
-CLARKSON: You'd scream.
Now, it is...
-Yep.

561
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,520
哎，别提了。听着，
你得学会装看不见。
Oh, no. Listen,
you have to block it out.

562
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,960
日子总还得
照样过下去嘛。
You just have to
get on with your life.

563
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:51,320
这怎么可能装看不见啊，
学校里其他那些妈妈
How can you
block it out when
all the other mothers

564
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:52,280
可都穿着薄纱睡裙呢！
are wearing negligees?

565
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:53,680
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

566
00:28:54,240 --> 00:28:55,920
“哎呀，不知道……”
"Oh, I wonder if..."

567
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,360
“不知道他今早会不会
开车来送孩子呢。”
"I wonder if he's doing
the school run this morning."

568
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:59,240
-“那我连晨袍
都懒得套了！”
-[笑]
-"I won't bother
with a dressing gown!"
-[LAUGHS]

569
00:28:59,280 --> 00:29:01,520
等我到了校门口，她们全都穿着涉水皮裤，
都提到这儿了！
I get down there, and they're
all in fishing waders,
up to here!

570
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:02,800
-不，其实……
-好吧。
-No, you know...
-Right.

571
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:04,520
你知道，我们家的情况是这样，
You know, what happens
in my house is that

572
00:29:04,560 --> 00:29:06,920
很多时候
我都得出远门工作拍片，
a lot of the time,
I'm away working
and filming something,

573
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:08,960
一离开家就是
好几个月。
away for a few months
at a time.

574
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,040
所以只要我一回家，
我就会把这当成头等大事，
And then,
when I do come home,
I make it a priority

575
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:14,040
要么送他们去学校，
要么接他们回家。
that I either take them
or I bring them home.

576
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:15,680
这也太崇高了吧！
That is so noble!

577
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,280
-这品质太崇高了，不是吗？
-[轻笑]
-That is so noble, isn't it?
-[CHUCKLES]

578
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,920
确实，我很喜欢接送他们。
I do. I like that very much.

579
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,800
-换我可懒得费这劲！
-[笑]
-I can't be bothered!
-[LAUGHS]

580
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,880
不过，这开车经验今天倒是帮了你大忙，
Still, it would have stood
you in good stead today,

581
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:26,520
因为毫无疑问，
你今天特意跑来开
我们的廉价车……
because, of course,
you came down here to drive
our reasonably priced car...

582
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:28,080
-没错。
-……绕着赛道跑了一圈。
-Yep.
-...round our track.

583
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:32,200
现在，来看看目前为止上过榜的名人。
Now, these are
the people who've been so far.

584
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:34,960
-乔迪·基德高居榜首，压在JK头上。
-对。
-We've got Jodie Kidd,
sitting at the top, above JK.
-Yeah.

585
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:38,320
然后在最底下垫底的，
是理查德·怀特利。
And then, at the bottom,
we've got Richard Whiteley.

586
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:40,880
想必，你肯定是冲着超过这里的罗斯·坎普来的吧。
Presumably, you'll be after
Ross Kemp, here.

587
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,400
坎普：行了，听着。
我可没数。
KEMP: All right, listen.
I do not know.

588
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,720
我心里一点底都没有。
I haven't got a clue.

589
00:29:43,760 --> 00:29:45,320
我就是把眼一闭，
大脚油门踩到底。
I shut my eyes
and put my toe down.

590
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:47,560
赛道外面到底是湿地
还是干地？
Was it wet
or was it dry out there?

591
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:48,960
呃，简直湿透了。
Well, it was soaking wet.

592
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,560
而且因为沥青路面上全是积水，
And because the water
was sitting on the tarmac,

593
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:53,240
反光晃得跟面镜子似的。
it was reflecting up
like a mirror.

594
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:55,360
根本看不清地上的行车线。
You couldn't really
see the markings.

595
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,960
你真该去当职业赛车手！
这完全就是……
You should be a racing driver!
This is exactly
the sort of thing...

596
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,400
-[大笑]
-……我们平时从那帮专业车手嘴里
听到的经典托词……
-[LAUGHING]
-...we hear from that lot
with their big...

597
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:04,840
话说回来，目前为止
我们的湿地最快纪录是罗斯·坎普。
Well, so far,
our fastest wet-runner
has been Ross Kemp.

598
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:05,960
坎普：好的，明白了。
KEMP: Right, okay.

599
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,760
所以，我得看能不能跑进1分54秒。
So, I'm looking at 1:54.

600
00:30:07,800 --> 00:30:10,320
你确实得瞄准1分54秒，
那才能成为最快……
You'd be looking
really at 1:54,
who would be the fastest...

601
00:30:10,360 --> 00:30:13,080
艾伦·戴维斯跑的时候只是微湿，明白吧？
This was mildly damp,
Alan Davies, okay?

602
00:30:13,120 --> 00:30:15,480
有谁想看看
马丁跑得怎么样吗？
Who'd like to have a look
how Martin did?

603
00:30:15,520 --> 00:30:16,760
-想看吗？
-观众：想！
-Yes?
-AUDIENCE: Yes.

604
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:18,040
好，那咱们来瞧瞧。
Okay, let's have a look.

605
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,240
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

606
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:21,760
克拉克森：
噢，这地确实挺湿的。
坎普：是啊。
CLARKSON:
Ooh, that is wet actually.
KEMP: Yeah.

607
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,720
克拉克森：鬼天气！
CLARKSON: Miserable day!

608
00:30:23,760 --> 00:30:25,360
坎普：你看，我都看不清标线了！
KEMP: See, I couldn't
see the markings!

609
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,640
克拉克森：
这借口你刚才用过了，
再换一个！
CLARKSON:
You've used that excuse,
now think of another one!

610
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:28,800
[坎普大笑]
[KEMP LAUGHS]

611
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:30,280
下雨天你都能把轮胎开出尖叫来！
You've got tyre squeal
in the rain!

612
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:34,120
-[轮胎尖叫]
-克拉克森：
这可不……这……
-[TYRES SQUEAL]
-CLARKSON:
That's not... That's...

613
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:36,040
-噢，失控了。
-没错，你冲出赛道了。
-Oh, I lost it.
-Yes. You were off.

614
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:38,840
好吧，确实冲出去了。
但也就稍微
滑大了一点点嘛。
Yeah, no, that's fair enough.
But that's just
sliding a bit wide.

615
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:40,280
-[哔——]
-克拉克森：什么？
-[BLEEP]
-CLARKSON: What?

616
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:41,800
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

617
00:30:45,040 --> 00:30:47,960
这段跑得非常棒！
我是说，史蒂夫·库根当时……
This is very good!
I mean, Steve Coogan was...

618
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,920
这儿车尾有点甩了。
That's sliding a bit
from the back.

619
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:52,320
跑得很不错。
对，最后稍微有点晃，
That's very good.
Yes, a bit wobbly at the end

620
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:54,640
穿过甘邦弯，
[激动地] 然后……
through Gambon corner
[EXCITEDLY] and...

621
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:56,080
[掌声]
[APPLAUSE]

622
00:31:05,520 --> 00:31:07,680
在揭晓成绩之前，
Just before
we reveal the time,

623
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:11,800
你在练习的时候，
可没这么顺顺当当，对吧？
wasn't completely
smooth out there
when you practised, was it?

624
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:13,560
可没刚才录像里这么顺。
Wasn't as smooth as that.

625
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:16,560
有谁想看看
他练习时出了什么洋相吗？
Who'd like to see
what happened
while he was practising?

626
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:17,680
观众：想看！
AUDIENCE: Yes.

627
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:19,520
放录像！
Put it on!

628
00:31:19,560 --> 00:31:20,960
克拉克森：噢，这是全场最难的一个弯。
CLARKSON: Ooh, it's
the hardest corner of the lot.

629
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,360
时速100英里穿针引线。
Threading the needle
at 100 miles an hour.

630
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:25,160
坎普：确实太难了！
克拉克森：然后……噢！
KEMP: It is hard!
CLARKSON: And... Ooh!

631
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,200
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

632
00:31:26,240 --> 00:31:27,920
克拉克森：漂亮！
CLARKSON: Very good!

633
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:33,160
-这……
-[掌声]
-That...
-[APPLAUSE]

634
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:44,040
这是所有人里滑出赛道滑得最远的一次！
That's the furthest
anybody's been from the track!

635
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:47,360
从来没人……
从来没人能一路失控
滑到那片柏油路上去！
Nobody...
Nobody's skidded off
onto that piece of tarmac.

636
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:49,560
-不过不管怎么说，来看看你的成绩。
-好。
-But anyway, your time.
-Yeah.

637
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:51,200
1分……这可是雨地圈，
One minute,
and it's a wet lap,

638
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:53,520
大家对这点都没异议，所以我们要贴上“W”。
and we're all agreed on that,
so we'll put the W on.

639
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:57,040
1分……惊不惊喜，意不意外，
One minute,
surprise, surprise,

640
00:31:57,080 --> 00:31:59,360
-跟罗斯·坎普一模一样！
-噢，不是吧！
-the same as Ross Kemp!
-Oh, no!

641
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:02,160
[坎普大笑]
[KEMP LAUGHS]

642
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:07,720
我确实觉得挺搞笑的，
I do think it's quite funny

643
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:09,120
你到处跟全世界吹
说加里是你亲兄弟。
you going around
telling the world
that Gary's your brother.

644
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,800
显然……
这简直不可思议！
Plainly...
This is unbelievable!

645
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:13,320
看来我得跟罗斯单挑一场了。
So, I need a showdown
with Ross then.

646
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:14,800
克拉克森：得，这两位想单挑。
CLARKSON: Well, these two
want a showdown.

647
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:16,920
他们还真想比一场。
They really want to
race each other.

648
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:20,680
-我觉得搞一场“坎普家族大决战”正合时宜。
-没错，绝对的！
-And I think a Kemp showdown
would be the order of the day.
-Yeah. Absolutely!

649
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:23,360
女士们先生们，
马丁·坎普！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Martin Kemp!

650
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:25,040
-谢谢大家。
-[掌声]
-Thank you.
-[APPLAUSE]

651
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:33,080
现在，想必大家都知道，
我们这节目向来不待见柴油车。
Now, as I'm sure you know,
we're not fans of diesel
on this programme.

652
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:35,840
我们一直觉得
那是撒旦才用的燃料。
We think it is
the fuel of Satan.

653
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:38,360
但今年夏天，
我开了一台这玩意儿。
But, in the summer,
I drove one of these.

654
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:41,640
奔驰E级
柴油轿车版。
The E-Class Mercedes
Diesel Saloon.

655
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:43,720
然后我发现了一件怪事。
And then I noticed
something strange.

656
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:46,480
数据都在这儿，看好了。
这是汽油版，
这是柴油版。
These are the figures, okay.
This is the petrol one,
this is the diesel.

657
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:49,600
柴油版马力更大，
零到六十英里加速一样。
The Diesel is more powerful,
same naught-to-60.

658
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:54,920
极速更快，省油得多，
还更便宜，而且据我观察，
居然没什么噪音。
Faster, much more economical,
cheaper, and as far as
I could tell, no noise.

659
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,320
这倒让我琢磨起来了。
And that got me thinking.

660
00:32:56,360 --> 00:33:00,000
说不定一直以来
在我戴着有色眼镜的时候，
Maybe, while I've been
wearing my blinkers,

661
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:01,520
