00:46:10,960 --> 00:46:12,800
克拉克森：
你看，问题就在这儿。
CLARKSON:
This is the problem, you see.

917
00:46:12,840 --> 00:46:14,960
不让人们喝酒，
后果就是这副德行。
This is what happens
when you don't
let people drink.

918
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:17,840
哈蒙德：什么玩意儿？
克拉克森：
那边发生什么了？
HAMMOND: What?
CLARKSON:
What's happened there?

919
00:46:17,880 --> 00:46:20,160
-哈蒙德：
噢，这下要遭殃了。
-他撞墙上了。
-HAMMOND:
Oh, that's gonna go wrong.
-He's gone into the wall.

920
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:22,440
-哈蒙德：
彻底玩砸了。
-你看，好端端一辆新车。
-HAMMOND:
That's gone very wrong.
-You see, a new car.

921
00:46:22,480 --> 00:46:25,480
克拉克森：所以你喝大后跑去街上，
把刚吞下的烤肉串
全吐成了“人行道披萨”。
CLARKSON: So, you go out
and you convert your kebab
into a pavement pizza.

922
00:46:25,520 --> 00:46:26,680
这麻烦可就惹大了。
That's big trouble.

923
00:46:26,720 --> 00:46:29,040
接着跟人干一架，
然后各回各家。
Then you have a fight,
then go home.

924
00:46:29,080 --> 00:46:32,600
-在我看来，沙特阿拉伯
可比这好玩多了。
-确实。
-Saudi Arabia looks to me
like a lot more fun.
-Yes.

925
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:35,280
-话虽如此，
你刚才爽翻了吧。
-那是相当爽。
-But that said,
you've had a laugh.
-I have.

926
00:46:35,320 --> 00:46:37,960
保时捷GT3，就在咱们的赛道上。
Porsche GT3 on our track.

927
00:46:42,960 --> 00:46:46,720
哈蒙德：
这身形宛如远古图腾，
早已融入了这片天地。
HAMMOND:
This shape is primeval,
part of the landscape.

928
00:46:46,760 --> 00:46:49,160
就像当年穴居人
一看到剑齿虎的轮廓
And just as
a caveman got the jitters

929
00:46:49,200 --> 00:46:51,880
就会吓得浑身发抖一样，
when he saw the outline
of a sabre-tooth tiger,

930
00:46:51,920 --> 00:46:55,840
我体内的出厂设定
也让我一看到这架势，
就忍不住直打哆嗦。
I'm pre-programmed
to start shaking
when I see this.

931
00:47:00,200 --> 00:47:01,640
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVS]

932
00:47:03,200 --> 00:47:04,640
[轮胎尖叫]
[TYRES SCREECH]

933
00:47:10,040 --> 00:47:14,120
那么，究竟是911家族里的哪一头猛兽，
正盘踞在咱们的赛道上巡猎？
So, which member
of the 911 species
is prowling around our track?

934
00:47:15,120 --> 00:47:16,920
它就是GT3。
This is the GT3.

935
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:22,120
一辆给你的配置更少、
却能带给你
更多极致享受的保时捷。
A Porsche that offers you less
so it can give you
so much more.

936
00:47:25,080 --> 00:47:27,120
它被彻底剥离了
所有讲究舒适的配置。
It's been stripped of
all creature comforts.

937
00:47:27,160 --> 00:47:30,960
所以没有车载导航，
没有空调，
隔音材料也大幅缩减。
So, there's no sat nav,
there's no air-conditioning,
less soundproofing.

938
00:47:31,000 --> 00:47:33,160
甚至连脚下的地毯都变薄了。
Even the carpets are thinner.

939
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:37,880
前排没有华而不实的真皮座椅，
后排更是
连个座儿都没给你留。
No fancy leather seats
in the front and
no seats at all in the back.

940
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:39,960
这一切，全都是打着
“减重”的大旗。
And it's all in the name
of saving weight.

941
00:47:43,960 --> 00:47:46,480
它从不为自己的偏执道歉。
It makes no apologies
for what it is.

942
00:47:46,520 --> 00:47:49,240
所以想要舒舒服服巡航？
换辆车吧。
So if you want a comfy ride,
get another car.

943
00:47:49,280 --> 00:47:52,320
大热天想吹凉风解暑？
换辆车吧。
If you wanna be cool
on a hot day?
Get another car.

944
00:47:52,360 --> 00:47:57,840
想要座椅高低调节功能？
虽然我根本不需要，
但也请换辆车吧！
If you want height adjustment
on the seats, which I don't,
get another car.

945
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:05,680
不过它留下的，
可全是硬核好料。
But what they've left behind
is good stuff.

946
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:09,720
举个例子，
瞧瞧这刹车。
For instance,
look at the brakes.

947
00:48:09,760 --> 00:48:12,000
卡钳是黄色的，
不是保时捷惯用的红色。
The callipers are yellow,
not the usual Porsche red.

948
00:48:12,040 --> 00:48:14,240
而这颜色意味着
一件极具分量的事。
And they signify
something important.

949
00:48:14,280 --> 00:48:16,480
刹车盘是碳陶瓷材质。
The discs are ceramic.

950
00:48:16,520 --> 00:48:19,800
听着像锅碗瓢盆的陶瓷，
但这意味着它们能经受住
极其残暴的折磨，
Sounds like pottery,
but it means they can cope
with enormous punishment

951
00:48:19,840 --> 00:48:21,720
绝不会出现过热
和热衰退。
without overheating
and fading.

952
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:25,720
再接着，就是这台引擎。
And then, there's the engine.

953
00:48:25,760 --> 00:48:30,000
噢，对，引擎！
它由钛合金等昂贵异域材料
手工纯打造。
Oh, yes, the engine.
It's hand-built from exotic
materials like titanium.

954
00:48:30,040 --> 00:48:32,960
可以说它很可能就是
这辆车上
最核心的部位。
And it's probably
the most important part
of the car.

955
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:37,080
这倒让人欣慰，
毕竟单这一台就得造价四万镑。
Which is good,
because it costs 40 grand.

956
00:48:37,120 --> 00:48:39,000
遗憾的是
Shame then

957
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:40,720
你根本就看不到它。
that you can't really see it.

958
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:44,240
它就窝在这儿某个角落，
藏在这台
老旧洗衣机后面。
It's in here somewhere.
Behind this
old washing machine.

959
00:48:46,920 --> 00:48:49,840
而且一想到它所在的位置，
我就觉得不可思议。
And it staggers me
when I think where it is.

960
00:48:49,880 --> 00:48:52,600
居然依旧孤零零地
悬空挂在车屁股的最外沿。
Still hanging out
over the edge at the back.

961
00:48:52,640 --> 00:48:54,720
从机械原理上讲，
这根本就是错的。
Now, technically
that's just wrong.

962
00:48:54,760 --> 00:48:58,960
这就好比盖金字塔，
尖头朝下立在地上。
It's like building a pyramid
with the pointy bit
at the bottom.

963
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:01,560
四十年前他们刚这么干时，
就是个蠢主意。
It was daft idea
when they first did it
40 years ago.

964
00:49:01,600 --> 00:49:04,440
在图纸上看，
今天它依然是个蠢主意。
And on paper,
it still is today.

965
00:49:04,480 --> 00:49:06,640
这车本该烂透了才对。
That should be rubbish.

966
00:49:09,480 --> 00:49:12,280
它本该耍起老款911
那些惯用的夺命阴招。
It should be up to
the usual old 911 tricks.

967
00:49:12,320 --> 00:49:15,880
车尾压着那么多分量，
甩起来就像个大钟摆。
All that weight at the back
swinging round
like a big pendulum.

968
00:49:15,920 --> 00:49:19,520
只要面前一没有大直道，
它随时准备收拾你。
Ready to punish you
the first time
you run out of straight road.

969
00:49:19,560 --> 00:49:20,960
顺便收拾你那点见底的车技。
And talent.

970
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:24,120
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

971
00:49:24,160 --> 00:49:28,080
按理说，过了这么多年，
他们总该试着把发动机悄悄往前挪挪。
So, you'd think
that over the years they'd try
and inch the engine forwards.

972
00:49:28,120 --> 00:49:29,920
[模仿德语口音]
“快瞧瞧我们漂亮的新大灯！”
[IN GERMAN ACCENT]
I say, "Look at
our lovely new headlamps".

973
00:49:29,960 --> 00:49:31,720
暗地里把发动机一点点往车头移。
Meanwhile the engine's
coming towards the front.

974
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:35,680
但并没有。德国工程师的字典里
可没有“掉头认错”这回事。
But, no. German engineers
don't do U-turns.

975
00:49:35,720 --> 00:49:37,560
所以它依然老老实实挂在屁股后头。
So, it's still out there
at the back.

976
00:49:44,640 --> 00:49:46,920
但不管它放在哪儿，
这台发动机简直神了！
Wherever it is though,
what an engine!

977
00:49:51,680 --> 00:49:53,200
数据摆在眼前：
Now, the figures
speak for themselves.

978
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:59,000
零到60英里加速4.5秒，
极速190英里每小时。
Naught to 60, 4.5 seconds,
top speed 190.

979
00:49:59,040 --> 00:50:02,240
难得的是，把这股猛力全踩出来，
居然一点都不吓人。
And for once, it's not scary
using all that power.

980
00:50:02,280 --> 00:50:04,040
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

981
00:50:04,080 --> 00:50:05,840
在过去那些可怕的老日子里，
为了克服操控上的硬伤，
In the bad old days,
to try and counter
the handling problems,

982
00:50:05,880 --> 00:50:08,160
保时捷试过各种荒唐简陋的笨招。
Porsche tried
crude Heath Robinson measures.

983
00:50:08,200 --> 00:50:11,760
他们往前保险杠里死命塞铅块，
试图以此平衡配重。
They stuffed
the front bumper with lead
to try and balance it.

984
00:50:12,640 --> 00:50:14,720
但全都没个卵用。
But none of it worked.

985
00:50:14,760 --> 00:50:18,680
在七八十年代，
911简直就是死神老爷的指定通勤车。
In the '70s and '80s,
the 911 was
the Grim Reaper's company car.

986
00:50:18,720 --> 00:50:21,160
环岛边上总能引来大批人群围观，
Huge crowds
would gather at roundabouts

987
00:50:21,200 --> 00:50:25,440
专门看发福的股票经纪人
开着保时捷“爬”上树梢。
to watch fat stockbrokers
climb trees in their Porches.

988
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:28,320
不过搁到现在，
他们可讲究科学多了。
Nowadays though,
they're a little more
scientific.

989
00:50:28,360 --> 00:50:32,360
他们把悬挂彻底吃透，
千锤百炼地打磨这台车，
They've mastered
the suspension and honed
and polished their car

990
00:50:32,400 --> 00:50:35,920
直到造出眼前这个
非凡的神作。
until they're left with this
magnificent creation.

991
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:39,160
[兴奋大笑]
[LAUGHING EXCITEDLY]

992
00:50:40,680 --> 00:50:43,280
这台机器简直不可思议！
This is an amazing machine!

993
00:50:43,320 --> 00:50:49,240
你想让它去哪它就去哪，
还能稳稳控住大角度的漂移！
You can put it
where you want it and then
hold it in huge slides!

994
00:50:49,280 --> 00:50:51,040
别担心，
我不会直接飘下悬崖的。
Don't worry,
I'm not gonna drift off.

995
00:50:52,440 --> 00:50:54,080
妈，瞧啊，我横着漂呢！
Look, Ma, I'm going sideways!

996
00:50:54,560 --> 00:50:56,120
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

997
00:50:56,800 --> 00:50:57,840
瞧瞧这个！
Look at that!

998
00:51:10,920 --> 00:51:13,760
发动机装错了地方？
是啊，那又怎样？
The engine's at the wrong end.
Yeah. So what?

999
00:51:15,800 --> 00:51:20,760
确实，这是个缺陷，
但这就好比辛迪·克劳馥脸上的美人痣，
Sure, it's a flaw.
But it's a flaw
like Cindy Crawford's mole.

1000
00:51:20,800 --> 00:51:22,920
或者J-Lo那夸张丰满的翘臀。
JLo's enormous buttocks.

1001
00:51:24,480 --> 00:51:26,560
这已经成了它
最标志性的特征。
It's become
its defining feature.

1002
00:51:26,600 --> 00:51:28,000
这正是这台车的
灵魂所在。
It's the whole point
of the car.

1003
00:51:32,280 --> 00:51:38,480
这台GT3绝对能够
盖棺定论地证明：
进化论是行得通的。
The GT3 is final
and absolute proof
that evolution works.

1004
00:51:38,520 --> 00:51:44,240
历经四十载，
它不仅是优秀，
这绝对是有史以来最棒的911。
And after 40 years,
this isn't just good.
This is the best 911 ever.

1005
00:51:50,320 --> 00:51:51,720
你知道吗，就这么定了！
Do you know, that's it?

1006
00:51:51,760 --> 00:51:52,880
我已经下定决心了，
彻底被说服了。
That has made up my mind.
I'm convinced.

1007
00:51:52,920 --> 00:51:54,520
我今晚一回家，
I'm gonna go
straight home tonight,

1008
00:51:54,560 --> 00:51:56,600
就把我那台老911的后座
和所有地毯全给扒了，
rip the back seats
and all the carpets
out my old 911

1009
00:51:56,640 --> 00:51:58,960
把它改造成这台车的迷你版。
太绝了！
and turn it into a mini
one of these.
It's fantastic!

1010
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:01,840
那根本行不通。你最后只会得到
一个连座儿都没有的倒扣大浴缸。
That won't work. You'll just
end up with an upturned
bathtub with no seats in it.

1011
00:52:01,880 --> 00:52:04,000
哈蒙德：你脑子绝对有坑。
HAMMOND: You are a
cuckoo job.

1012
00:52:04,040 --> 00:52:06,560
不过，我今年开过这台车，
你们知道我骨子里算个法拉利粉。
However, I've driven this
this year, and you know
I'm a bit of a Ferrari man.

1013
00:52:06,600 --> 00:52:08,080
踢球的暴发户！
Footballer!

1014
00:52:08,120 --> 00:52:12,200
对。但这台GT3是我今年开过最棒的车。
Yeah. This was the best car
I've driven all year, GT3.

1015
00:52:12,240 --> 00:52:15,440
我从没想过
自己会对一台911给出这种评价。
我爱死它了。
I never thought
I'd say that of a 911.
I adored it.

1016
00:52:15,480 --> 00:52:17,600
很高兴听你这么说。
它确实棒极了。
I'm glad to hear you say.
It is absolutely fantastic.

1017
00:52:17,640 --> 00:52:21,560
不过当然了，它还剩最后一项终极测试。
那就是：斯提格。
But, of course, there is
just one test left for it.
The Stig.

1018
00:52:21,600 --> 00:52:25,360
在我们把他派去“无敌号”航母之前——
大家稍后就能看到了——
Now, before we sent him off
to HMS Invincible,which we'll
see in a short while,

1019
00:52:25,400 --> 00:52:28,080
为了让他热热身，
毕竟外面正下着倾盆大雨，
as a bit of practise,
because it is bucketing
out there,

1020
00:52:28,120 --> 00:52:30,400
我们让他开着这台车
上了赛道。
we sent him out
on the track in this.

1021
00:52:30,440 --> 00:52:33,360
所以，快点，快点冲吧，
斯提格巴赫先生！
So, schnell, schnell,
HerrStigbacher!

1022
00:52:33,400 --> 00:52:35,160
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVS]

1023
00:52:35,200 --> 00:52:37,080
哈蒙德：他出发了！
HAMMOND: And he's off!

1024
00:52:37,120 --> 00:52:39,320
赛道地面完全湿透了。
瞧瞧那水花！
Now, the track surface
was soaking.
Look at that spray!

1025
00:52:39,360 --> 00:52:42,440
所以待会儿场面上
绝对会相当“欢脱”。
So this is gonna be
very lively out there.

1026
00:52:42,480 --> 00:52:45,200
小心点，斯提格。稳住。
Be careful, Stig. Steady.

1027
00:52:45,240 --> 00:52:47,320
[背景音乐响起：《Through the Barricades》]
[THROUGH THE BARRICADES
PLAYING]

1028
00:52:47,360 --> 00:52:50,960
哈蒙德：哎呀。
我觉得斯提格是在拍
马丁·坎普的马屁呢。
HAMMOND: Oh, dear.
Stig's sucking up to
Martin Kemp I think.

1029
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:52,800
真不要脸。
Shameless.

1030
00:52:52,840 --> 00:52:54,920
现在过芝加哥弯了。
瞧啊，他真的在……
Now, we go round Chicago.
And look, he really is...

1031
00:52:54,960 --> 00:52:58,920
他真得拼了老命
才能把这台GT3
按在跑道上。
He really is having to work
to keep the GT3
in check here.

1032
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:01,360
马上要切入锤头弯了。
Going to be going
into the Hammerhead.

1033
00:53:01,400 --> 00:53:04,360
这绝对是目前为止
最大的考验。
Now, this could be
the biggest test so far.

1034
00:53:04,400 --> 00:53:06,920
你甚至能肉眼看到
动力全开时车头翘了起来。
You can actually see
the front end lifting
under the power.

1035
00:53:06,960 --> 00:53:10,880
今天这种鬼天气根本就不适合开后置引擎的车！
This is not a day
for a rear engine car at all!

1036
00:53:10,920 --> 00:53:13,640
在那种赛道上，后置引擎绝对要命。
Definitely not a day for
a rear engine car out there.

1037
00:53:13,680 --> 00:53:15,440
雨天开这玩意儿太难了！
That is so difficult
in the wet!

1038
00:53:15,480 --> 00:53:17,960
全油门冲出穿梭弯……
完蛋，他要失控了！
Blasting out
of the Follow Through...
No, he's gonna lose it!

1039
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:19,360
[轻笑] 抓稳了，
斯提格宝！
[CHUCKLING] Hang on there,
Stiggy!

1040
00:53:19,400 --> 00:53:22,400
-[音乐继续播放]
-瞧瞧那架势。
-[SONG CONTINUES PLAYING]
-Look at that.

1041
00:53:22,440 --> 00:53:24,200
连汗
都没出一滴。
Not even
breaking into a sweat.

1042
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:26,480
最后两个弯了。
他能稳住
不滑上草地吗？
The last two bends now.
Is he going to
keep it off the grass?

1043
